{"id": "lobby-money-to-the-measure", "title": "Lobby money traced: votes don’t follow it; sponsoring clients’ deals does, on thin numbers", "seconds": 136.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "40f07ccaaf66bff5", "words": 417, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "A lobbyist is someone paid to win over City officials. So let’s follow that money, step by step.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.81, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Client", "sub": "pays a lobbyist"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Lobbyist", "sub": "contacts officials"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Official", "sub": "votes or sponsors"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Measure", "sub": "helps the client?"}], "kicker": "Follow the money"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.73, 0.86, 1.2, 1.49, 1.61, 1.86, 2.09, 2.33, 3.42, 3.62, 3.87, 4.19, 4.37, 4.81, 5.11, 5.26]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "amount"], "text": "First, how much did clients pay San Francisco lobbyists since 2010?", "t0": 5.93, "t1": 9.78, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Paid to lobbyists", "sub": "January 2010 to October 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.51, 0.71, 0.86, 1.27, 1.51, 1.68, 2.15, 2.57, 2.82, 3.14]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "About 173.3 million dollars.", "t0": 9.78, "t1": 12.59, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "about $173.3 million", "label": "from 2,520 clients"}, "emph": ["173.3"], "wt": [0.04, 0.34, 0.51, 0.85, 1.41, 1.66, 1.91, 2.26]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding. And the main answer may surprise you.", "t0": 13.11, "t1": 16.97, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.31, 0.39, 0.88, 1.08, 1.14, 2.07, 2.26, 2.36, 2.6, 2.93, 3.1, 3.58]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The Ethics Commission, the City’s rule enforcer, has fined lobbyists in 12 cases since 2012.", "t0": 17.19, "t1": 22.39, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Ethics Commission penalties", "sub": "lobbying cases since 2012"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.51, 0.95, 1.04, 1.37, 1.59, 2.22, 2.43, 2.77, 3.28, 3.37, 3.71, 4.16, 4.44, 4.76]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "58,168 dollars in all. The largest was 16,000.", "t0": 22.51, "t1": 27.47, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Ethics Commission penalties", "sub": "lobbying cases since 2012"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.53, 1.0, 1.18, 1.5, 2.02, 2.38, 2.5, 3.18, 3.35, 3.82, 3.97, 4.44]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "It also fined 13 of 36 officials or their committees, 207,033 dollars.", "t0": 27.59, "t1": 32.71, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Penalties on officials", "sub": "22 cases, 13 of 36 officials"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.45, 0.75, 1.18, 1.27, 1.75, 2.28, 2.44, 2.6, 3.07, 3.26, 3.51, 3.76, 4.13, 4.58]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The largest, 108,180 dollars, involved Mark Farrell’s campaigns.", "t0": 32.83, "t1": 38.01, "shot": "b5a", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$108,180", "label": "the largest penalty", "sub": "Mark Farrell’s campaigns"}, "emph": ["108,180"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.81, 1.03, 1.35, 1.57, 2.02, 2.2, 2.5, 2.77, 3.27, 3.74, 4.01, 4.41]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "No prosecutor’s file names a sitting official.", "t0": 38.13, "t1": 40.26, "shot": "b5b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "No sitting official", "sub": "named in any prosecutor’s file"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.73, 1.05, 1.28, 1.36, 1.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "The first lead is who pays. The top payers: Prologis, 2.7 million dollars.", "t0": 40.48, "t1": 45.41, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Largest lobbying clients", "rows": [["Prologis", "$2.7 million"], ["Recology", "$2.5 million"], ["Golden State Warriors", "$2.5 million"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.6, 0.7, 0.87, 1.79, 1.95, 2.22, 2.78, 3.41, 3.59, 3.85, 4.11, 4.43]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[5]"], "text": "When a client’s circle gave money to a supervisor, did that supervisor vote the client’s way more often?", "t0": 45.63, "t1": 50.75, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Do votes follow the money?", "kicker": "The big test"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.21, 0.63, 0.97, 1.19, 1.44, 1.55, 1.61, 2.23, 2.38, 2.57, 3.14, 3.35, 3.43, 3.81, 3.97, 4.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[5]"], "text": "With money: 95.5 percent.", "t0": 50.75, "t1": 53.63, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["circle gave money", "95.5%"], "b": ["circle did not", "91.5%"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.27, 0.78, 1.35, 1.58, 1.83]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[5]"], "text": "Without money: 91.5 percent. Why so close?", "t0": 53.63, "t1": 57.16, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["circle gave money", "95.5%"], "b": ["circle did not", "91.5%"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.41, 0.84, 1.33, 1.56, 1.8, 2.69, 2.98, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[5]"], "text": "Because nearly every money vote passes anyway, with no one voting no.", "t0": 57.16, "t1": 60.59, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["circle gave money", "95.5%"], "b": ["circle did not", "91.5%"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.32, 0.62, 0.92, 1.14, 1.39, 1.81, 2.22, 2.43, 2.6, 2.77, 3.11]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["story[5]", "story[13]"], "text": "No more than chance.", "t0": 60.71, "t1": 61.8, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["No", "more", "than", "chance."], "sub": "96.4% of money files pass with no one voting no"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.39, 0.56]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead is who sponsors a bill, meaning who carries it.", "t0": 62.42, "t1": 65.32, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["contacted by a lobbyist", "26.9%"], "b": ["not contacted", "17.5%"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.44, 0.67, 0.78, 0.93, 1.4, 1.47, 1.84, 2.12, 2.27, 2.66]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "Supervisors a lobbyist contacted sponsored 26.9 percent of the time. Others, 17.5.", "t0": 65.44, "t1": 71.91, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["contacted by a lobbyist", "26.9%"], "b": ["not contacted", "17.5%"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.73, 0.8, 1.25, 1.83, 2.3, 2.85, 3.12, 3.35, 3.69, 3.77, 3.87, 4.72, 5.31, 5.86, 6.12]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "But lobbyists go first to supervisors already likely to carry a bill.", "t0": 72.03, "t1": 75.37, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "who is approached as much as who is persuaded"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.64, 0.83, 1.1, 1.19, 1.85, 2.21, 2.54, 2.63, 2.93, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead is the one real gap.", "t0": 75.59, "t1": 77.34, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Money files naming a client", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "136 passed contracts, leases and deals"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 0.66, 0.79, 0.9, 1.11, 1.37]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "136 passed deals named a client who was paying a lobbyist.", "t0": 77.46, "t1": 81.38, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Money files naming a client", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "136 passed contracts, leases and deals"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.53, 1.12, 1.47, 1.86, 2.07, 2.13, 2.56, 2.67, 2.81, 3.16, 3.23]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "When that client’s circle had given to a supervisor, how often did that supervisor sponsor the deal?", "t0": 81.5, "t1": 86.19, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Money files naming a client", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "136 passed contracts, leases and deals"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.3, 0.68, 0.98, 1.1, 1.35, 1.46, 1.53, 2.15, 2.35, 2.64, 2.75, 2.92, 3.48, 3.9, 4.0]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "23.8 percent.", "t0": 86.19, "t1": 87.94, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "23.8%", "label": "against 8.8% for other supervisors", "sub": "against 8.8 percent"}, "emph": ["23.8"], "wt": [0.04, 0.72, 1.01, 1.24]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Other supervisors: 8.8 percent. That’s beyond chance. But it rests on just 21 cases.", "t0": 88.46, "t1": 94.76, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "5 against 1.5 expected"}, "emph": ["21 cases"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 1.09, 1.32, 1.58, 1.79, 2.68, 2.96, 3.34, 4.36, 4.54, 4.64, 4.9, 5.02, 5.22, 5.71]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Six measures named the client in the deal itself: 3 were contracts worth up to 187.3 million.", "t0": 94.98, "t1": 101.48, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "After the vote", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "51 passed measures"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.79, 1.0, 1.07, 1.44, 1.52, 1.6, 1.83, 2.86, 3.2, 3.39, 3.87, 4.17, 4.33, 4.47, 4.65, 4.97, 5.52, 5.78, 6.03]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "Of 34 clients with City payments, 27 got paid more afterward.", "t0": 101.6, "t1": 105.46, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "After the vote", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "51 passed measures"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.7, 1.12, 1.27, 1.54, 2.02, 2.62, 2.81, 3.06, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Still, a deal is usually worked out by a department before the Board votes.", "t0": 105.58, "t1": 109.11, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "negotiated by a department before the Board votes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.6, 0.75, 0.99, 1.11, 1.4, 1.64, 1.79, 1.92, 1.98, 2.42, 2.73, 2.81, 3.07]}, {"scene": "lead6", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "The fifth lead is late reports.", "t0": 109.33, "t1": 110.9, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2026-01-15", "to": "2026-02-15", "days": "", "fromLab": "report due", "toLab": "report arrives late", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.64, 0.77, 0.99]}, {"scene": "lead6", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "Lobbyists must report contacts by the 15th of the next month.", "t0": 111.02, "t1": 114.17, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2026-01-15", "to": "2026-02-15", "days": "", "fromLab": "report due", "toLab": "report arrives late", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.53, 0.73, 1.06, 1.63, 1.76, 1.86, 2.35, 2.48, 2.57, 2.82]}, {"scene": "lead6", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "3,039 reports came in late.", "t0": 114.29, "t1": 116.57, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2026-01-15", "to": "2026-02-15", "days": "", "fromLab": "report due", "toLab": "report arrives late", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.59, 1.06, 1.5, 1.74, 1.89]}, {"scene": "lead6", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "178 contacts were first reported after the final vote.", "t0": 116.69, "t1": 120.21, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Disclosed after the vote", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "178 contacts about 25 Board files"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.5, 1.05, 1.61, 1.77, 2.01, 2.47, 2.72, 2.81, 3.15]}, {"scene": "lead6", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "A late report is a filing slip. But no one watching that vote could see them.", "t0": 120.33, "t1": 124.33, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Disclosed after the vote", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "178 contacts about 25 Board files"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.36, 0.73, 0.85, 0.91, 1.31, 2.06, 2.27, 2.4, 2.56, 2.92, 3.1, 3.36, 3.54, 3.72]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Nothing here shows money given in return for an official act.", "t0": 124.55, "t1": 127.33, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Any payment for an official act", "Fees that depended on the outcome", "Contacts by unregistered lobbyists"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.56, 0.85, 1.1, 1.36, 1.45, 1.81, 1.95, 2.0, 2.42]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The fee agreements, and bank records that only investigators can demand.", "t0": 127.45, "t1": 132.31, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Fee agreements between clients and lobbyists"}, {"who": "", "what": "Bank records, which only investigators can get"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.28, 0.59, 1.3, 1.47, 1.7, 2.3, 2.5, 2.76, 3.14, 3.32, 3.53, 4.18, 4.36]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has ruled on it.", "t0": 132.43, "t1": 133.92, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.7, 0.84, 1.12, 1.26]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 134.04, "t1": 135.96, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.38, 0.48, 0.53, 0.96, 1.13, 1.21]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · who pays", "lead2": "The big test · votes", "lead3": "Lead 2 · who sponsors", "lead4": "Lead 3 · 23.8%", "lead5": "Lead 4 · after the vote", "lead6": "Lead 5 · late reports", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "contrast"}